addrlib's x86 AVX2 swizzle path (host image copies, unused by compute) dispatches with
__builtin_cpu_supports, whose __cpu_model Zig's compiler runtime does not provide: build
addrlib without SIMD on x86 (the portable path). docs/specs/hermetic-build.md, phase 4.

--- a/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build
+++ b/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build
@@ -52,6 +52,6 @@
 
 # The SIMD path in addrlib only supports x86 and Aarch64 (NEON).
-if host_machine.cpu_family() in ['x86', 'x86_64', 'aarch64']
+if host_machine.cpu_family() in ['aarch64']
   cpp_args_addrlib += '-DADDR_ALLOW_SIMD=1'
 endif
 
